 "what_this_set_does_and_does_not_test": "the package is natively x2 and its LQ is already resampled to the GT geometry, so taking LR = LQ/4 puts a synthetic x4 on top of the real degradation. Measured: the LQ loses 25.8 dB through a 1/4 round trip (so the x4 does discard real content) while the degraded MTF sits only 0.03-0.11 in L2 from a synthetic x4 control measured the same way -- inside the 0.21 that generalised fine. This set therefore stresses real CONTENT much more than it stresses real DEGRADATION. mvsr4x remains the harder operator test.",
