 "readings": [
  "we win on fidelity and on detail direction: PSNR +0.739 dB median (better on 46/50), LPIPS -0.0248 (43/50), null cosine +0.097 (49/50), and p8.terr_null -1.273 (47/50).",
  "we lose on flicker: 0.537 against 0.414, worse on 42/50, the same direction as on heldout.",
  "this set corrects a generalisation drawn from mvsr4x. There, all three generative arms scored BELOW bicubic in PSNR (ours -0.84). Here ours is ABOVE bicubic (+0.196 dB median, better on 35/50) and FlashVSR+ is below it (-0.443), so \"generative restoration loses to bicubic on real degradation\" is specific to mvsr4x, where bicubic is close to a no-op because the LQ already carries only ~1/4 of the resolution. It is not a general property of real degradation."
 ]
